## Closing answer

"I model User, Group, Expense and Split, with split types as strategies – equal, exact and percent – that always return shares adding up exactly to the total in paise, giving leftover paise by a fixed rule. `ExpenseService` records an expense and updates a pairwise `BalanceSheet`; net balances always sum to zero. Settlements are just entries in the opposite direction. To settle up, a greedy simplifier matches the biggest debtor with the biggest creditor using two heaps, giving at most n − 1 payments – simple, though not always the theoretical minimum. Edits are reversals plus new expenses, so history stays explainable."
